{"episodes":{"187815":"A historic tornado event for Wisconsin as the first documented tornado occurred in the month of February. An approaching cold front and upper level disturbance initiated the severe thunderstorms from late afternoon into the early evening.  An EF-1 tornado occurred in Green County near Juda/Albany and then a second tornado developed which was stronger and produced EF-2 level damage.  The long track tornado impacted 30 houses and numerous barns and outbuildings.  Only 1 injury occurred when the tornado hit someone driving a car near Hwy 14 and Territorial Rd.  A high volume of hail also occurred with these storms, but the largest hailstone were generally just at or above severe levels.","188711":"Severe thunderstorms brought large hail to parts of Arkansas on February 9, 2024.","189086":"A cluster of mostly sub-severe thunderstorms during the evening of the 8th produced isolated instances of severe hail and wind along and south of I-80.","189088":"A cluster of mostly sub-severe thunderstorms during the evening of the 8th produced a couple of instances of severe hail in northwest Indiana.","189090":"A cluster of mostly sub-severe thunderstorms during the evening of the 8th moved offshore over Lake Michigan where a severe wind gust was recorded.","189277":"A brief landspout tornado was reported through social media over rural areas of Finney county. A few photos of the landspout were taken.","189433":"A long-lived low pressure system churned from the Central to Northern Plains February 7th through February 8th. Initial impacts in southeast Minnesota were limited to rain until the evening of the 8th when a narrow line of strong storms provided nickel sized hail in Cazenovia (Richland County)."},"events":[{"begin":"2024-02-09T00:07Z","county":"Jefferson","damageCrops":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-02-09T00:17Z","endLat":42.9263,"endLon":-88.9041,"episode":187815,"id":1154238,"injuries":0,"lat":42.8895,"location":"1.84 WSW Busseyville","lon":-89.013